| phase-41 | `DONE` | B1-NET-02 (HIGH) fixed (see `workspace/phase-41/REPORT.md` + `docs/security-report.md:815`). Confirmed-pairing gate for LocalSend sends. New pure-JVM `services/localsend/LocalSendPairing.kt`: `LocalSendPairing.gate` refuses any receiver that announces `protocol:"http"` (or no TLS fingerprint) and any device whose fingerprint was never paired; `LocalSendPairing.startPairing` derives a deterministic 6-digit out-of-band code (`LocalSendPairingCodes.pairingCode`) + formatted fingerprint; `confirmPairing`/`pair` persist a TOFU anchor (constant-time code compare, `ConstantTime.stringEqual`) into a `LocalSendPairedDeviceStore` (`InMemoryLocalSendPairedDeviceStore` for tests; `SettingsLocalSendPairedDeviceStore` + `SettingsManager.localsend_paired_<fp>` for production). `LocalSendSender` now gates `sendFile` BEFORE any network I/O (`LocalSendSender.kt:313-326`) and pins every payload to the stored paired fingerprint, refuses non-`https` payload URLs in `openConnection`, and the announce never advertises `protocol:"http"` (`LocalSendMessages.senderIdentity` = `"https"`, `LocalSendProtocol.kt:107`). `LocalSendSendDialog` requires an explicit pairing (code typed from the receiver — verified constant-time, mismatch refuses — OR an explicit "fingerprints match" acknowledgement, `LocalSendSendDialog.kt:158-199`) before a device is sendable, and a per-send confirmation before every transmission — a `200` to `/prepare-upload` is documented + treated as ZERO evidence of human consent. Tests: `LocalSendPairingTest` (19) + `LocalSendProtocolTest` (25); `gradle testDebugUnitTest` 924 green + `gradle assembleDebug` green (1 pre-existing flaky `PluginUpdateEngineTest` timing failure that passes in isolation — unrelated to this diff, per phase-40 report). |
| phase-42 | `DONE` | B1-NET-03 (HIGH) fixed (see `workspace/phase-42/REPORT.md` + `docs/security-report.md` B1-NET-03 row). Plugin update trust anchor moved into the APK — the manifest can no longer set `downloadUrl`/`sha256`/`pinnedCertHash` out of nothing. New `plugins/runtime/CompileTimePluginPinStore.kt`: per-plugin compile-time release pins (`PinnedPluginRelease` id → version → {sha256, pinnedCertHash}), `PinVerdict`, download-host allow-list (`DEFAULT_DOWNLOAD_HOSTS = {DEFAULT_MANIFEST_HOST}`) with `isHostAllowListed` host gate (lowercase + trailing-dot folded, port ignored), and the production `CompileTimePluginPins.RELEASES` EMPTY ⇒ fail closed (no downloadable plugin shipped yet); all digest compares via `ConstantTime.hexEqual`. Wired as defense-in-depth at THREE independent gates: `PluginUpdateChecker.check` offers only compile-time-pinned values (`plugins/runtime/PluginUpdateChecker.kt`), `PluginUpdateEngine.update` re-verifies the persisted target against pins BEFORE any byte moves or rollback-root write (`plugins/runtime/PluginUpdateEngine.kt:110-116`), and `PluginDownloader` now refuses any artifact host not on the allow-list before connecting (`allowedDownloadHosts` param, `plugins/runtime/PluginDownloader.kt`). `PluginStoreController` threads pins into both check calls (`plugins/store/PluginStoreController.kt`). Surviving `PluginUpdateInfo` carries the compile-time pin digests, not the wire's casing/text. Tests: new `CompileTimePluginPinStoreTest` (10) + new B1-NET-03 cases in `PluginUpdateCheckerTest` (5), `PluginUpdateEngineTest` (1, unpinned/re-pinned refused before any byte moves), `PluginDownloaderTest` (2, host allow-list), `PluginUpdateStoreFlowTest` (1, forged offer refused); the documented flaky `PluginUpdateEngineTest#a hash mismatch…` test was made deterministic (tampered served payload can never match the pin — was zip-timestamp clock-tick dependent). `gradle testDebugUnitTest` 943 green + `gradle assembleDebug` green. |
| phase-43 | `DONE` | B1-DB-1 (HIGH) fixed (see `workspace/phase-43/REPORT.md` + `docs/security-report.md` B1-DB-1 row). Corrupt-open classifier narrowed to genuine corruption only: `NoteflowDatabase.kt` `isDatabaseCorruptException` matches `android.database.sqlite.SQLiteDatabaseCorruptException`, `net.zetetic.database.sqlcipher.SQLiteNotADatabaseException`, and the messages "file is not a database"/"malformed"/"database disk image is malformed" — a lock-contention/disk-I/O/ENOSPC `SQLiteException` subclass is NO LONGER classified as corruption, so a transient hiccup can never quarantine a healthy vault. Quarantine no longer auto-creates an empty replacement DB: `SafeSupportSQLiteOpenHelper` rethrows after quarantine and a `throwIfVaultQuarantined` guard fails every further open while the persistent flag is set, so an empty vault is created only after the user's explicit "start fresh". `NoteflowViewModel` surfaces `CorruptionRecoveryScreen` in-session (not just on the next launch), gates the six Room-backed note flows on `authenticated && !corruptionBlocked` (`.catch { emit(emptyList()) }` so a discovery race can't crash a collector), resets+re-runs initialization after start-fresh, and clears the corruption flag after a successful restore so the post-restart open isn't guard-blocked. Tests: new `CorruptionClassifierTest` (10); `gradle testDebugUnitTest` 953 green + `gradle assembleDebug` green. |
| phase-44 | `DONE` | B1-DB-4 (HIGH) + B1-AUTH-06 (MEDIUM) fixed — SAME root cause (see `workspace/phase-44/REPORT.md` + `docs/security-report.md` B1-DB-4/B1-AUTH-06 rows). Note bodies no longer exist as PLAINTEXT files: the field-encrypted `pages.extractedText` column is the ONLY body store. New pure-JVM `services/NoteBodyVaultPolicy.kt` classifies note-body sources (text/-typed + `.md`/`.txt` only — PDF/image/attachments untouched) and resolves/delete-legacy-file policy. New single write path `NotePageDao.updatePageBody` + `NoteRepository.updatePageBody` (AES-GCM per-record AAD). MainActivity (both layouts) now reads `resolveBodyForDisplay` and saves via new `viewModel.saveMarkdownNoteBody`; the `File.writeText` plaintext editor writes and their NonCancellable plumbing are deleted. Text imports (HomeScreen md/txt/docx, `ImportExportService` HTML/ZIP/Obsidian pass-2) and journal/daily/wiki page creation store `sourceFilePath = null` + body in `extractedText`. Readers (`WikiLinkParser.readFullText`, `BacklinksInspector` convert-to-wikilink, `DocumentTextExtractor`) follow the column. One-time `NoteRepository.migrateLegacyPlaintextNoteBodies` sweeps pre-fix file bodies into the encrypted column then deletes the files (undecryptable pages + failed deletes keep their file; flag `SettingsManager.noteBodyPlaintextMigrated` only set on completion); WAL checkpointed + DB HMAC re-stamped after mutation. `MarkdownPreviewScreen` baseDir falls back to the imports dir so relative markdown images keep resolving. Tests: new `NoteBodyVaultPolicyTest` (12); `gradle testDebugUnitTest` 965 green (0 failures) + `gradle assembleDebug` green. No schema change, no migration, no new deps, `.github/workflows/` untouched. |
| phase-45 | `DONE` | B1-CRYPTO-02 (HIGH) fixed (see `workspace/phase-45/REPORT.md` + `docs/security-report.md` B1-CRYPTO-02 row). The vault DEK is no longer obtainable without the password: `SecurityService` (`services/SecurityService.kt`) now persists the device-wrapped DEK copy behind an internal `DekDeviceStore` seam (`SharedPrefsDekDeviceStore` = prefs `noteflow_keystore`/`noteflow_sec_dek`; `clear()` uses `commit()`, disk-acknowledged, and drops the stale `dek_auth_required` flag); `readDek()` fails closed (absent or `authRequired=true` blob ⇒ null) and `getOrCreateDek` never mints over an auth-gated blob. Pure-JVM `services/DekAtRestPolicy.kt` (decision table) is wired as `NoteflowViewModel.enforceDekAtRestPolicy()` into `setMasterPassword` (after the wrapped-DEK commit), `changeMasterPassword`, `verifyMasterPassword` (every password unlock), `verifyBiometricsAndUnlock`, and `setBiometricEnabled` — biometrics OFF ⇒ `clearDek()` so the ONLY at-rest wrapper is the password-derived KEK; biometrics ON ⇒ repersist ONLY `authRequired=true`. The pre-fix `setBiometricEnabled(false,…)` non-auth re-wrap is deleted. `SecurityService(context)` call sites → `SecurityService.forDevice(context)` (`NoteflowViewModel.kt:115`, `NoteflowDatabase.kt:345`). Tests: new `DekAtRestPolicyTest` (4) + `B1Crypto02DekAtRestTest` (9, incl. a source-level wiring pin); `gradle testDebugUnitTest` 978 green (0 failures) + `gradle assembleDebug` green. No schema change, no migration, no new deps, `.github/workflows/` untouched. Related-but-out-of-scope: factory re-derive + locked-open gap = B1-AUTH-02 (phase-47), silent DEK re-mint = B1-CRYPTO-05 (phase-64), API 26-29 biometric downgrade = B1-CRYPTO-07 (phase-65) — none touched here. |
| phase-46 | `DONE` | B1-AUTH-01 (HIGH) fixed (see `workspace/phase-46/REPORT.md` + `docs/security-report.md` B1-AUTH-01 row). Downloadable-plugin bytecode can no longer reach the vault DEK in-process — two independent gates. (1) Runtime sandbox: pure-JVM `plugins/runtime/PluginFrameworkClassLoader.kt` becomes the plugin `DexClassLoader`'s parent (`services/AppClassLoaderFactory.kt:34`); `isAppPrivateForbidden` (`:70-71`) refuses EVERY `com.authorss81.noteflow.*` class outside the `plugins.*` framework surface (incl. `Class.forName` reach-through), while `java.*`/`kotlin.*`/`android.*`/third-party classes still delegate. (2) Verify-time content gate: pure-JVM `plugins/runtime/ArtifactStaticScan.kt` runs inside `ArtifactSignatureVerifier.verify` (`:76-81`), the single funnel for install / every load re-verify / update / rollback; it structurally parses `.class` constant pools + DEX `string_ids`/`type_ids` and byte-searches other entries, rejecting app-private prefixes (`services|data|ui|theme|utils`), bare secret-bearing names (`VaultKeyHolder`, `EncryptionService`, `NoteflowDatabase`, `SettingsManager`, `NoteRepository`, `SecurityService`) and raw `java.net`/`javax.net.ssl` egress primitives. Phase-46 review closed all 5 review findings in-tree: net-egress + `ProcessBuilder`/`Runtime` now matched in slash AND dot form (`Class.forName("java.net.HttpURLConnection")` literals refused), sensitive names matched ONLY as whole tokens (benign lookalike identifiers pass), and a source-level pin (`PluginBytecodeIsolationTest`) holds that `plugins.*` host code never references a vault-handle type. Tests: `PluginBytecodeIsolationTest` (20); `gradle testDebugUnitTest` 1001 green (0 failures) + `gradle assembleDebug` green. No schema change, no migration, no new deps, `.github/workflows/` untouched. Out-of-scope (documented): native `System.loadLibrary`, `sun.misc.Unsafe` and a separate `:remote` process option.
| phase-47 | `DONE` | B1-AUTH-02 (HIGH) fixed (see `workspace/phase-47/REPORT.md` + `docs/security-report.md` B1-AUTH-02 row). The lock is now enforced at the DATA LAYER. `NoteflowViewModel.lock()` (`NoteflowViewModel.kt:2543-2549`) — when a master password exists — now cancels the section/page observer jobs, calls `NoteflowDatabase.dispose()` (closes + forgets the Room/SQLCipher instance so NO keyed handle survives; previously it zeroized only `VaultKeyHolder`), marks `databaseDisposedByLock`, and resets `dataInitialized` so the next unlock re-establishes observers. The stale-handle/fresh-open exploits both fail closed: a stale handle hits a closed connection pool, and `NoteflowSqlcipherFactory.create` (`NoteflowDatabase.kt:343-371`) routes the `dek == null` open through the new pure-JVM `services/LockedOpenGuard.kt` — a password-protected vault with no in-memory DEK THROWS `IllegalStateException("Vault is locked: database key not available")` BEFORE any `getOrCreateDek()`/persisted-copy access, while a passwordless vault still re-reads its device-wrapped copy (the boot credential by design). Explicit unlocks (`verifyMasterPassword` `:2080`, `verifyBiometricsAndUnlock` `:2220`) reinstate the live connection via `reinstateDatabaseAfterLock()` (no-op unless lock() disposed it) BEFORE the dbGate flows flip on, and an open failure there is zeroized and returned — never counted as a wrong password. `onCleared()` also disposes. Tests: `LockedOpenGuardTest` (3) + `B1Auth02LockedOpenTest` (9, incl. a fake-repository model proving no key is ever re-created on a locked open + source-level wiring pins); `gradle testDebugUnitTest` 1013 green (0 failures) + `gradle assembleDebug` green + `gradle assembleRelease` green. No schema change, no migration, no new deps, `.github/workflows/` untouched. Related-but-out-of-scope: in-flight save writes with zeroized key = B2-UI-1 (phase-49), plugin lifecycle hooks running before unlock = B1-AUTH-03 (phase-67). |
| phase-48 | `DONE` | B2-LOG-01 (HIGH) fixed (see `workspace/phase-48/REPORT.md` + `docs/security-report.md` B2-LOG-01 row). Crash logging is single-owner. `utils/AppStartupLogger.kt` is a startup-EVENT timer only: the crash handler it installed at `:38-42` (which ran OUTERMOST = FIRST because MainActivity registers PrivacyCrashReporter first) and the raw `logCrash`/`printStackTrace` → `Log.e` dump at `:55-77` are deleted, and the `Log.e(TAG, msg, e)` failure paths (which would print an exception's trace) no longer pass the exception object (`appendToFile` `:61`, `clearLogs` `:86`). `services/PrivacyCrashReporter.kt` is the SOLE `UncaughtExceptionHandler`; its `logUncaughtException` (`:53-55`) routes through the new pure-JVM `crashLogEntry` (`:64-71`, sanitized message + scrubbed `class.method(file:line)` frames, no raw trace) and writes to the local file only — never logcat. Repo-wide source pin: `setDefaultUncaughtExceptionHandler` appears only in `PrivacyCrashReporter.kt`. Tests: new `B2Log01CrashReportingTest` (6, incl. sanitization/scrub behavior + source pins); `gradle testDebugUnitTest` 1019 green (0 failures) + `gradle assembleDebug` green (first invocation had an unreproducible transient failure; all re-invocations fully `UP-TO-DATE` green with the 173.6 MB debug APK on disk). No schema change, no migration, no new deps, `.github/workflows/` untouched. Out-of-scope (documented): `app_startup.log` size cap/rotation = B2-LOG-02 (phase-70); B1-PLAT-5 (path-regex namespace gap) was planned for phase-89 but CLOSED in this phase's review fix — `sanitizeMessage` now redacts any `/data/user/<uid>/...` or `/data/data/...` path (covers namespace + real applicationId dir), pinned by a new test. |
